cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "A trained network, checked by Lean"
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 kernel-checked theorems about small neural networks: a trained one-layer transformer
  (integer weights, exact real softmax) and a trained two-layer MLP that add modulo 113 on all
  12,769 inputs; an alpha-beta-CROWN certificate for ACAS Xu network 1_1, property 1; a
  Mathlib theorem that fixed-phase cosine networks add modulo p for every p >= 3; and a trained
  recurrent adder correct on inputs of every length.
authors:
  - family-names: Lince
    given-names: Thomas
repository-code: "https://github.com/teal-sea/lean-checked-network"
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-10-15
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - neural networks
  - modular arithmetic
